        <mxCell id="vQJH2k5jHzZeBWDmTKOx-47" value="This architecture uses a single website for both the portfolio and the CMS. Anyone can go to all justinslijkhuis.nl/** URLs except for justinslijkhuis.nl/cms/** which requires an access token. The access token can be achieved using justinslijkhuis.nl/cms/login which you wil navigate to by default if you aren&#39;t logged in. Logging in returns an access token together with a refresh token which will both quickly invalidate. All database operations are done on the server-side of the website. The portfolio part will only execute SELECT statements. The CMS part will execute all CRUD statements if the given access token is valid.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Advantages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ All UI components are in the same website making it more easy to build and work with the visual posts section.&lt;br&gt;+ Makes deployment easier since I would only need to host a website and a database.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ Project can be completed way faster compared to implementing something like a REST API as well.&lt;br&gt;+ Only having a single website and a single database makes this architecture very cheap.&lt;br&gt;+ Allows SQL queries to be written specificaly for a page making the query as optimized as possible.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Disadvantages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Handling security on the server-side of the website based on the URL could bring some challenges that puts the security at risk.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Issues on the CMS part of the website could break the entire website which will result in the Portfolio being offline.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- The database connection details are closer to the client-side when compared to a REST API which could put those secrets at risk.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="50" width="750" height="260" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
