        <mxCell id="vQJH2k5jHzZeBWDmTKOx-73" value="This architecture uses a single website for both the portfolio and the CMS. The website uses a REST API for data operations. Anyone can go to all justinslijkhuis.nl/** URLs and send a GET request to all justinslijkhuis.nl/api/** endpoints. The only limitation is that an access token is required for requests to justinslijkhuis.nl/api/cms/** and that justinslijkhuis.nl/cms/** also requires an active access token to be able to retrieve the pages.. The access token can be achieved using justinslijkhuis.nl/cms/login which you wil navigate to by default if you aren&#39;t logged in. The login page uses a login endpoint to validate the passwords and generate an access token together with a refresh token which will. both quickly invalidate. The API requests can be done both on the client-side and server-side of the website.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Advantages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ All UI components are in the same website making it more easy to build and work with the visual posts section.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ Security can be really good since a REST API (framework) allows for better security and validation in an easier manner.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Disadvantages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Deployment is a harder since there is now also a REST API to release and manage.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Takes more time building the portfolio and CMS since a REST API needs to be created from scratch.&lt;br&gt;- There is still the challenge of validating the access token based on the cms/** route to retrieve the pages.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Data can be gathered more easily outside of the website unless server-side token is used or domain validation is added.&lt;br&gt;- Increases latency and costs by adding an extra HTTP request to loading pages.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- The entire website will not work anymore if the REST API crashes since it is very data dependant.&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="866" y="51.5" width="750" height="268.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vQJH2k5jHzZeBWDmTKOx-74" value="Spring Boot REST API" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1466" y="589.5" width="150" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vQJH2k5jHzZeBWDmTKOx-75" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.99;exitY=0.082;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;exitPerimeter=0;" parent="1" source="vQJH2k5jHzZeBWDmTKOx-56" target="vQJH2k5jHzZeBWDmTKOx-74" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
