        <mxCell id="vQJH2k5jHzZeBWDmTKOx-104" value="Performs SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE statements" style="ellipse;shape=cloud;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacingLeft=20;spacingRight=20;spacingTop=5;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1994.5" y="863" width="205" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vQJH2k5jHzZeBWDmTKOx-105" value="This architecture uses one website for the portfolio and one website for the CMS splitting their responsibilities. Anyone can go to justinslijkhuis.nl/** which is the portfolio website. If someone goes to the CMS website located at cms.justinslijkhuis.nl/** , then they are required to have an access token. The access token can be achieved using cms.justinslijkhuis.nl/login which you wil navigate to by default if you aren&#39;t logged in. Logging in returns an access token together with a refresh token which will both quickly invalidate. All database operations are done on the server-side of the website. The portfolio website will only execute SELECT statements. The CMS website will execute all CRUD statements if the given access token is valid.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Advantages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ Security can be applied on the entire CMS website so there is no need for route based security.&lt;br&gt;+ Issues with the CMS website do not bother the portfolio website allowing it to continue operating if the CMS crashes.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ The portfolio website can be scaled separately if that is something that might be needed in the future.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ Allows SQL queries to be written specificaly for a page making the query as optimized as possible.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Disadvantages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Handling security on the server-side of the website based on the URL could bring some challenges that puts the security at risk.&lt;br&gt;- UI components aren&#39;t in the same website which makes it hard managing the visual posts section of the website.&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Deployment is a bit harder compared to architecture 1.0 since there is now two websites to release and manage.&lt;br&gt;- The database connection details are closer to the client-side when compared to a REST API which could put those secrets at risk.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1693" y="50" width="750" height="260" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vQJH2k5jHzZeBWDmTKOx-107" value="Architecture 3.1" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontStyle=1;fontSize=25;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1967" y="1180" width="200" height="30" as="geometry" />
