        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vQJH2k5jHzZeBWDmTKOx-191" value="Improved variant of architecture 3.2 which moves the components to the Portfolio website. The CMS website will retrieve the components using module federation. This allows both websites to have the same components at all times meaning no inconsistencies while also making sure the Portfolio website always works. It also decreases complexity for development and releases since it doesn&#39;t require an extra container.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Advantages compared to 3.2&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ The websites don&#39;t need to update dependencies meaning it is always up to date causing no inconsistencies between posts.&lt;br&gt;+ Doesn&#39;t require an extra container for components which decreases both development and deployment complexity&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Disadvantages compared to 3.2&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;- Post part of the CMS doesn&#39;t work if the components can&#39;t be retrieved from the Portfolio website, but that is not that big of an issue.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;- Adds the complexity of working with module federation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
