        <mxCell id="JXyWXwS42iE2nbsT7plQ-25" value="Performs SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE statements" style="ellipse;shape=cloud;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;spacingLeft=20;spacingRight=20;spacingTop=5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2821.5" y="863" width="205" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="JXyWXwS42iE2nbsT7plQ-26" value="Combination of architecture 3.3 and 2.1. This splits the website into the portfolio and CMS part. Both websites use the same GraphQL API which uses the PostgreSQL database.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Advantages compared to 3.3&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ Improved security like the ability to implement rate limiting, fight against SQL injection, etc.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Advantages compared to 2.1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ The portfolio will still works if the CMS crashes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Disadvantages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;- The portfolio will break if the GraphQL server breaks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;- GraphQL and module federation introduce more complexity.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- GraphQL and Redis introduce more costs.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Post part of CMS doesn&#39;t work if the portfolio doesn&#39;t work.&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
